      "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\sqrt{((5^2-4) \\div 3)-2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations,\n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses, and\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents.\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(({5}^{2}-4)÷3)-2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{((25-4)÷3)-2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(21÷3)-2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7-2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
